  "limits": [
    "The 66 constructor bound is for a root without an arbitrary-depth surrounding wire context. Context lifting can add constructors/data.",
    "The factor twenty counts rewrite occurrences, including inverse uses. It does not bound total Track/Cell constructors, bytes, generation/checking time, context data or machine runtime.",
    "Expansion is equational and may use formal inverse pure-wire laws; no forward-only simulation or termination theorem follows.",
    "The added higher definition schema takes one contextual old Step. It is bounded in boundary rewrite uses but retains arbitrary wire-context payload. Derivation solely from eleven context-free root definitions and existing mixed-context lifting is not yet proved.",
    "These higher definition generators extend a partial higher basis. No full finite higher-basis completeness or unconditional prior-basis derivability is claimed.",
    "Expanded boundary tracks have no old wire labels; their higher comparison internals may still use old-library generators. No projection of the whole higher calculus to a smaller old-free basis or higher conservativity is proved.",
    "The stateful repair result is endpoint kernel equality within the updated checked model, not a code-changing compiler comparison or a new cryptographic/runtime bound.",
    "Ordinary shared proofs may use the same bounded macros; no intrinsic higher-dimensional size or speed separation is demonstrated.",
    "Remaining structural/crypto/internal-wire overlaps, complete execution including oracle internals, quantitative reduction integration, fair total costs and primary-theorem novelty remain open."
  ],
